#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/id #uuid "0f1a2a41-b97f-5ac7-a51d-a90cb3ba366a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12368" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} \\int_{0}^{3-x-y} x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x-y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-x-y}x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x\\cdot [z]_{z=0}^{z=3-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x(3-x-y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x-{x}^{2}-xy\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3x-{x}^{2})y-\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-{x}^{2})(x-0)-\\frac{1}{2}x({x}^{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3}\\,dx & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =8-6 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197963 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "2ad7b82c-8624-5a59-8a2c-c5c1852e6cf6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12389" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2} \\int_{-1}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} x^2y+xz^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}y+x{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}y+x{z}^{2}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{[{x}^{2}yz+\\frac{x{z}^{3}}{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y(1-0)+x(\\frac{1}{3}-0)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}]}_{x=-1}^{x=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}y({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3})+\\frac{1}{6}({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{y}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(6+1)-(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197964 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "5a596157-d6dd-528d-912c-52889780567d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12390" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle  \\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the domain of integration $R = [1,2] \\times \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right] \\times [1,4]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{x}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{dx}{x}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy{\\int }_{1}^{4}dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}dz & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]_{1}^{2}\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot (4-1) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0)\\cdot (0+1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x = 3\\ln 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf0dd2b6-4b08-5b1a-8cc5-947c37241514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339296} {:answer/id #uuid "57c1813d-68d4-53cd-92ac-a20c8da44331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339297} {:answer/id #uuid "bee916ac-becc-5fd6-8660-d1341a4b5669" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339298} {:answer/id #uuid "bab21f6e-1100-524b-921f-3ef0f21225f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339299} {:answer/id #uuid "a6434375-41ba-5b1f-9fa6-60cd1abac7d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bee916ac-becc-5fd6-8660-d1341a4b5669" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339298} :answer-field/id #uuid "49ebd11c-67c5-503d-82af-d77c05c7da2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339295}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f5e6d22-78e1-5ce4-8774-243957052edf" :question/math-academy-id "q-161268" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" :question/worked-solution "Since the domain of integration $R=[-1,2]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]\\times [-1,-\\frac{1}{2}]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz & =[{x}^{2}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{z}]}_{-1}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =(4-1)\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fba8fc24-d55e-510e-807f-4e0e198013d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339303} {:answer/id #uuid "55e9f940-26c0-522e-8910-5223844cb48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339304} {:answer/id #uuid "892a83b2-0074-58c6-a55b-c8a962189b5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339305} {:answer/id #uuid "45adaf99-f894-52de-a887-98e553f8d0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339306} {:answer/id #uuid "0e60d8ae-21f4-5c97-9423-087af7e11390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "892a83b2-0074-58c6-a55b-c8a962189b5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339305} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8a821d-ac07-5baa-832d-724b52496102" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a63e2e9-2448-54c3-b3d8-fdee5b0324b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161270" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,4]\\times [1,2]\\times [0,1]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(8-0)(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{7}{3})(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,\\text{d}z & =(4-0)\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{14}{3}-2=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84fa3fb9-7644-5eeb-bc0b-228933b1783f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339310} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ad8361-ea25-5065-bd8d-15e507e0344f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339311} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd71b78-8234-5b59-8b5a-63908a62fc3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339312} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd0e6a2-bd99-52a1-a68a-f337709a1722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339313} {:answer/id #uuid "7b02b17a-b4d8-554b-85a8-9c31efaeb3a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddd71b78-8234-5b59-8b5a-63908a62fc3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339312} :answer-field/id #uuid "85d1a52d-1c0c-588e-8fda-e4366ee15169" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "210d7977-9e37-5020-af7b-0f4146ca5c57" :question/math-academy-id "q-161271" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{3}-2z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,1]\\times [0,2]\\times [-1,1]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2z\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & =[{x}^{3}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot [{y}^{4}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2z\\,\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot [{z}^{2}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{3}-2z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=4-32-0=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da8146ce-a08f-5f67-ac27-a97eae98a918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339317} {:answer/id #uuid "0dfbfb9c-aadb-5c1c-a7ab-232aa117ad5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339318} {:answer/id #uuid "e598e9ec-9e6c-5dd5-a84e-bf61234cb861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339319} {:answer/id #uuid "5faca2f0-cc7e-5594-a520-c2bec85608e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339320} {:answer/id #uuid "1d47b230-deb6-5423-98db-f2c9cd9d29ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da8146ce-a08f-5f67-ac27-a97eae98a918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339317} :answer-field/id #uuid "790c2068-47c4-54dd-9fcb-f29688fd52c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91eb91a5-3e61-525e-9079-82513656bb56" :question/math-academy-id "q-161299" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)]_{z=0}^{z=\\pi }\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+0))\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy\\,dx & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}(-0+1)\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx & =-2{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb6554de-ce09-5696-84da-98541a098048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339324} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb498eb-d29f-5951-ad8b-719d7b360291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339325} {:answer/id #uuid "704facb4-869a-5d8d-bfbc-fb2af2e59247" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339326} {:answer/id #uuid "a73c913f-521e-5d7e-a8b5-f9e6d9137563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339327} {:answer/id #uuid "64416db3-d31b-5de2-b60b-85b3b198e3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cb498eb-d29f-5951-ad8b-719d7b360291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339325} :answer-field/id #uuid "17dea7ae-b8ce-5400-abdc-6581ef64c6af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d98f6ecc-b6d7-51ed-8008-c37499e79fdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161307" :question/problem "${\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{y}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}4x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,1]\\times [1,2]\\times [2,5]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot [{y}^{3}]_{1}^{2}\\cdot (5-2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (8-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}z & =[2{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot (5-2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{y}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z=21-6=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1836eac-767f-591d-b21c-382aec6bba1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4e+2\\pi -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339331} {:answer/id #uuid "3718d87a-9db8-5cf6-8b55-b103291bcc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2e+\\pi -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339332} {:answer/id #uuid "f7404756-e9b7-5a32-a06b-229efd69ab7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-3\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339333} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ed68f4-8af4-5f10-8478-b795a059c1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(-e-2\\pi +3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339334} {:answer/id #uuid "641e2e60-3cd5-557f-b478-4f6010fb11c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e-\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3718d87a-9db8-5cf6-8b55-b103291bcc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2e+\\pi -2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339332} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e3e2eb9-d1a7-5546-a818-9eea5e0f651c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b2c42e6f-ccd5-5e9d-8551-e0fc1128d810" :question/math-academy-id "q-161308" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{y}{z})\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{y}{z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,2]\\times [1,e]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\text{d}z & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =(1+1)\\cdot 2\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =4(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =(\\pi -0)\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡|z|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{y}{z})\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x=4(e-1)+2\\pi =2(2e+\\pi -2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87f7d4bb-e197-5148-a4ff-74e335b6bed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339338} {:answer/id #uuid "28c5d0ee-e166-5026-b843-18e218358dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339339} {:answer/id #uuid "d2868bdd-5f75-52b5-b52f-c1e3ca229c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339340} {:answer/id #uuid "3f67fd06-c5e5-5c94-9b31-4524f8409406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339341} {:answer/id #uuid "79ae7ea0-f430-5907-bddc-33dbcd301ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87f7d4bb-e197-5148-a4ff-74e335b6bed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339338} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5565aa3-c87e-5f93-8b68-1d1262a0bcd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9facc126-f11d-55c7-9b6e-94ca30cb30d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161310" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{z}({y}^{2}-x)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{z}({y}^{2}-x)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{z}{y}^{2}-{e}^{z}x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}-x{e}^{z}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}(9-0)-x{e}^{z}(3-0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}9{e}^{z}-3x{e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}9{e}^{z}-3x{e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}(9-3x)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(9-3x)[{e}^{z}]_{z=0}^{z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(9-3x)(2-1)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}9-3x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}9-3x\\,dx & ={[9x-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(18-6)-(9-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a8fe609-7b83-5540-9d6c-6250a9a9655d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339345} {:answer/id #uuid "40546de5-3018-50e9-a063-6d5b8d548b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339346} {:answer/id #uuid "5105a4dd-0c57-5cca-a7d6-9b7ff23aa444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339347} {:answer/id #uuid "d65131e4-66ee-5f6b-a9f6-e4c6184370cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339348} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3d947b-592d-5c20-bc3a-e777ce21b83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5105a4dd-0c57-5cca-a7d6-9b7ff23aa444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339347} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8bd4817-cd8f-5002-aee5-5d85b1d2b1d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "348609bf-a73c-5077-8bf6-502af54128f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161313" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{[\\frac{(x-y)^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z[x]_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(0-y)^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z(1-0)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}[z]_{z=0}^{z=2\\pi }+[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]_{z=0}^{z=2\\pi })\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}}{3}(2\\pi -0)+(-1+1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-y)^{3}+{y}^{3}\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{[-\\frac{(1-y)^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}((-0+\\frac{1}{4})-(-\\frac{1}{4}+0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b3f6023-d2ca-50a1-9e37-3b369c02efb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339352} {:answer/id #uuid "e6fbf335-1150-529f-8313-3bd66e3e78d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339353} {:answer/id #uuid "1f599054-00d9-566b-b249-8c567132469c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339354} {:answer/id #uuid "6d70befa-17d3-551a-a0eb-6be49060c074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339355} {:answer/id #uuid "f23de2b7-908c-568d-af99-27c45e54434e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d70befa-17d3-551a-a0eb-6be49060c074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339355} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4c2a71-dd8d-5e72-8a5b-2fb50451d51b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af2a76d4-12a8-5320-b18a-a9fa3f9cd47d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161330" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y+z)]_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+y+z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+y+z)\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+z)\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+z)\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+z)\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+z)]}_{y=0}^{y=z}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(z+z)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2z+z)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+z)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+z)\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3z-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2z+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3z+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]}_{z=0}^{z=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}+0+0]-[-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "361fada9-6a34-52c8-acc7-667bbe1c4d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339359} {:answer/id #uuid "2275d1d1-d3e9-56c9-93db-94c085831533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339360} {:answer/id #uuid "b8932db8-a7d9-5ea7-9e9b-c94a2c150dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339361} {:answer/id #uuid "69125116-f268-5aa1-90bb-27ec48eb8158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339362} {:answer/id #uuid "d68711cf-c0de-5380-bda1-3d564dfb8d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2275d1d1-d3e9-56c9-93db-94c085831533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339360} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd68650-afb5-56d9-b7a8-b5c2db1edd98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "522a89a8-07d1-5532-b0d2-e1ca72387334" :question/math-academy-id "q-161336" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}z}\\frac{z}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}z}\\frac{z}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}z}\\frac{z}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{[z\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{z})]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{3}z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{z})]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{3}z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[\\frac{\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{y}dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{3}[z]_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,y\\,dy & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088c9f0c-217a-5b18-83d2-6d5f3b247f1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339366} {:answer/id #uuid "a663717b-5bb9-5578-adf4-2fcce983a3d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} {:answer/id #uuid "1f2e0454-2d06-527c-a9bd-fe7609743d68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339368} {:answer/id #uuid "5de3081a-84b5-59ed-8b4d-657be642c3d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339369} {:answer/id #uuid "8e609c24-3880-5f0f-bb9b-c981c16a63e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a663717b-5bb9-5578-adf4-2fcce983a3d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf2ab592-73f3-5056-8e95-1f53e805cc99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "037e0349-4f50-53d6-b9f2-1f9b278844be" :question/math-academy-id "q-161344" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}}\\frac{x}{z}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}}\\frac{x}{z}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}}\\frac{x}{z}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{x}{z}\\cdot z\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})]}_{y=0}^{y={z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{z})]}_{y=0}^{y={z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]_{z=0}^{z=\\pi /2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x(-0+1)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}x\\,dx & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88970e4d-f54f-5484-b730-94f8fadd1366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197630} {:answer/id #uuid "c243b024-2af1-58aa-89f2-12d11c7f9ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197631} {:answer/id #uuid "e06d748a-7e07-581a-9661-ba0029ce01eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197632} {:answer/id #uuid "5f10e338-3bb8-5158-bad2-5c8f254ba031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197633} {:answer/id #uuid "75ea090a-55ba-5410-bc1b-8fd6ad53db75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f10e338-3bb8-5158-bad2-5c8f254ba031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197633} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2d2ccaf-6ed3-5944-89e9-da594761ca27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5259e1b9-028d-504a-ac38-55eae4d0c29a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39476" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy+yz+xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+z)x+yz\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y+z)\\,{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2}+yz[x]_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y+z)(2-0)+yz(2-0)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$, treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(y+z)+2yz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(1+z)y+2z\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}((1+z)[{y}^{2}]_{1}^{2}+2z[y]_{1}^{2})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}((1+z)(4-1)+2z(2-1))\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3(1+z)+2z)\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3+5z)\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3+5z)\\text{d}z & ={[3z+\\frac{5}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3(1-0)+\\frac{5}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e436e4c-d41e-518b-9651-41098f85c5d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{119}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339373} {:answer/id #uuid "2d33cfd2-bc43-5380-aa5d-976100d85170" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339374} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3d4a60-c868-5283-8142-95bb536e6644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{68}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339375} {:answer/id #uuid "a82ea2d5-7b17-5dd7-9a43-58eebd13be5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{136}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339376} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a25b97-0d11-5841-b7d0-1b3cf8623bc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{132}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a82ea2d5-7b17-5dd7-9a43-58eebd13be5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{136}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339376} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d18db64-db45-5d18-bbf4-ed4acd00e320" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d53082b5-3230-55a2-93ba-6d81e864ec6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-40205" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{x}^{2}yz]_{x=0}^{x=y+z}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}(y+z)^{2}yz\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}(y+z)^{2}yz\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}z+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}{z}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=z}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{5}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{5}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{17}{12}{z}^{5}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{17}{12}{z}^{5}\\,dz & ={[\\frac{17}{72}{z}^{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{72}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =\\frac{136}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a0e67df-35e6-5cdf-98c7-f9ac6652be88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339380} {:answer/id #uuid "444433be-f6e0-5cfa-b782-8a1550be38ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339381} {:answer/id #uuid "83fdbded-12dc-5933-9fd7-62912fe15108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339382} {:answer/id #uuid "1d83ebfd-0601-597f-9b43-73822de8ee12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339383} {:answer/id #uuid "448f42ab-5731-5996-b3ff-58bfb99ed2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83fdbded-12dc-5933-9fd7-62912fe15108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339382} :answer-field/id #uuid "e76cd8e3-7f76-5e4b-979c-4737dd0d1296" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba800b66-75ce-562f-aaca-1cc5c61cfefa" :question/math-academy-id "q-40497" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{x+z}72xyz\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{x+z}(72xyz)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36xz[{\\int }_{0}^{x+z}2y\\,dy]dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36xz[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=x+z}\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36xz(x+z)^{2}\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36{x}^{3}z+72{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+36x{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $z$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}36{x}^{3}z+72{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+36x{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}36{x}^{3}z+72{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+36x{z}^{3}\\,dx]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[9{x}^{4}z+24{x}^{3}{z}^{2}+18{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}51{z}^{5}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}51{z}^{5}\\,dz & ={[\\frac{17{z}^{6}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37994fdb-8818-54b2-8856-73c3e8191ea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339387} {:answer/id #uuid "33e4e32b-71d8-52ae-abe7-e78c65efb746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339388} {:answer/id #uuid "17b7bfb4-6b65-5597-85f3-b8693e0f13d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339389} {:answer/id #uuid "1a29cb2e-3219-5985-bc14-8b6b8eeea9a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339390} {:answer/id #uuid "08981e8e-f53b-59a8-95e5-3a7e472f1453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37994fdb-8818-54b2-8856-73c3e8191ea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339387} :answer-field/id #uuid "c837daa7-9791-58ee-9414-9126d838aaba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf718b0c-73d8-54ff-8b64-3e23755e9364" :question/math-academy-id "q-82852" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and write our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,1]\\times [0,2]\\times [-1,1]$ is a rectangular box, and each integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our sum of repeated integrals as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z\\,+\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate each of these separately:\n\n- For the first product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot (2-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}z & =(1-0)\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{16}{3}=\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
